<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Where two lines meet in a triangle</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>In triangle OAB, \(\overrightarrow{OA} = \mathbf{a}\) and \(\overrightarrow{OB} = \mathbf{b}\). C is on OA with \(OC : CA = {@r1@} : {@s1@}\). D is on AB with \(AD : DB = {@r2@} : {@s2@}\). The lines OD and BC meet at X, with \(\overrightarrow{OX} = h\,\overrightarrow{OD}\) and \(\overrightarrow{BX} = k\,\overrightarrow{BC}\).</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Triangle OAB with C on OA and D on AB; dashed lines OD and BC cross at X. Not to scale.">
[[jsxgraph width="420px" height="300px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [-0.6, 5.6, 8.6, -0.8], axis: false, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  var lo = {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false};
  var po = {fixed: true, highlight: false, size: 2, fillColor: '#000000', strokeColor: '#000000', withLabel: false};
  var tx = {fixed: true, highlight: false, useMathJax: false, fontSize: 15};
  // triangle OAB, fixed positions (not to scale)
  var O = [0, 0], A = [7.5, 0.6], B = [2.6, 4.8];
  b.create('segment', [O, A], lo); b.create('segment', [O, B], lo); b.create('segment', [A, B], lo);
  b.create('text', [-0.45, -0.25, 'O'], tx); b.create('text', [7.7, 0.5, 'A'], tx); b.create('text', [2.45, 5.2, 'B'], tx);
  function at(P, Q, t) { return [P[0] + t*(Q[0]-P[0]), P[1] + t*(Q[1]-P[1])]; }
  // C on OA, D on AB, X where OD meets BC (fixed positions, labels only)
  var C = at(O, A, 0.6), D = at(A, B, 0.4);
  var ds = {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 1.5, dash: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false};
  b.create('segment', [O, D], ds); b.create('segment', [B, C], ds);
  // X: solve O + h(D - O) = B + k(C - B)
  var d1 = [D[0], D[1]], d2 = [C[0] - B[0], C[1] - B[1]], det = d1[0]*(-d2[1]) + d2[0]*d1[1];
  var h = (B[0]*(-d2[1]) + d2[0]*B[1]) / det, X = [h*D[0], h*D[1]];
  b.create('point', C, po); b.create('point', D, po); b.create('point', X, po);
  b.create('text', [C[0] - 0.1, C[1] - 0.4, 'C'], tx); b.create('text', [D[0] + 0.15, D[1] + 0.1, 'D'], tx);
  b.create('text', [X[0] + 0.12, X[1] + 0.3, 'X'], tx);

})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div><div>(a) \(\overrightarrow{OD} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) \(\overrightarrow{BC} =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>Give \(h\) and \(k\) as fractions.</p><div>(c) \(h =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><div>(d) \(k =\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div><p>(e) We may equate the coefficients of \(\mathbf{a}\) and \(\mathbf{b}\) because</p><div>[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) By the ratio theorem, \(\overrightarrow{OD} = {@tOD@}\). (b) \(\overrightarrow{OC} = {@c1@}\,\mathbf{a}\), so \(\overrightarrow{BC} = \overrightarrow{OC} - \overrightarrow{OB} = {@vBC@}\).</p><p>Two routes to X: \(\overrightarrow{OX} = h\,\overrightarrow{OD} = {@al@}h\,\mathbf{a} + {@be@}h\,\mathbf{b}\), and \(\overrightarrow{OX} = \overrightarrow{OB} + k\,\overrightarrow{BC} = {@c1@}k\,\mathbf{a} + (1 - k)\mathbf{b}\).</p><p>Because \(\mathbf{a}\) and \(\mathbf{b}\) are not zero and not parallel, neither can make up for the other, so the coefficients must match: \({@al@}h = {@c1@}k\) and \({@be@}h = 1 - k\).</p><p>(c), (d) Solving, \(h = {@h@}\) and \(k = {@kx@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
