  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors II: where two lines meet in a triangle</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.6: Find where two lines in a triangle meet by writing one point two ways in terms of a and b and equating coefficients.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 10 in Exercise B of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: a triangle with randomised division ratios instead of a trapezium, scaffolded in five parts with the reason for equating coefficients, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
